{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0ETA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{T_j \\to T\\}_{j = 1, \\ldots, m}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{T_{ji} \\to T_j\\}_{i = 1, \\ldots n_j}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\{T_{ji} \\to T\\}_{i, j}$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-composition-standard-V}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f0306d730eedf194c3ecd8f132bedddddd446ec0d91a8caa8b9fef8eeb704cd0", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4e7e4510a42a7b5b10717aa0e3e765d32389572a19f318fcb1a5f47fd05e8d1c", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an affine scheme. Let <MATH_0002>\nbe a standard V covering. Let <MATH_0003>\nbe a standard V covering. Then <MATH_0004>\nis a standard V covering.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9e3f83fa4cdc5df61502ad5d355d8557a1436e6daf5ae5cb7ebc43c721e22ef2", "unit_id": "tag:0ETF:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0ETA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$V \\subset W$", "MATH_0002": "$W \\subset \\Omega$", "MATH_0003": "$V \\subset \\Omega$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:e67a6ea9b187dd1fe9eb735cb22e7f5eea673b60ab302982a5a05b42e9eb1f97", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e8b1f3a0804f79f87a99b68a707408aa3d1eb1d8ca73f2739daebf5766279b50", "source_text": "This follows formally from the observation that if\n<MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002> are extensions of\nvaluation rings, then <MATH_0003> is an extension\nof valuation rings.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5726b3361137ec365243105e46f3d4129d69ea428533d8e3828cb5e3b0892ef7", "unit_id": "tag:0ETF:proof"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "0ETA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$\\{T_j \\to T\\}_{j = 1, \\ldots, m}$", "MATH_0003": "$T_j$", "MATH_0004": "$j$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{T_j \\to T\\}_{j = 1, \\ldots, m}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\{T_j \\to T\\}_{j = 1, \\ldots, m}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\{\\coprod_{j = 1, \\ldots, m} T_j \\to T\\}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-refine-standard-V}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:ccb2fb6bf39d129da2166eb9742b53dcf2e16a8ba2f6fd15e832015162d52201", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:64b969156ab66ece7ea32cf967c4f52ef6644cf6043c5fb3fc10cc8efa901ad9", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be an affine scheme. Let <MATH_0002>\nbe a family of morphisms with <MATH_0003> affine for all <MATH_0004>.\nThe following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0005> is a standard V covering,\n<STRUCT_0003> there is a standard V covering which refines\n<MATH_0006>, and\n<STRUCT_0004> <MATH_0007> is a standard\nV covering.\n<STRUCT_0005>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3d14cdac056ae42b4cb80aaed0e5a8b6ee5a85e94f3d2331e685ecd3bea49575", "unit_id": "tag:0ETG:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "0ETA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\coprod_{j = 1, \\ldots, m} T_j$", "MATH_0002": "$T_j$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4d9a900c7a7b16cfdcecc4eb4e5f02a405a1e6e2217a25b62056c2fd0fe3490d", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c5e8992d3be1ffb146f01b8545937254f3feeb2ed6cd2556fb4a11b91a7280c7", "source_text": "Omitted. Hints: This follows almost immediately from the definition.\nThe only slightly interesting point is that\na morphism from the spectrum of a local ring into\n<MATH_0001> must factor through some <MATH_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:be659200c62f82474826d7a8697bbc746dd5fe20b25164f6aa414b7f968e1401", "unit_id": "tag:0ETG:proof"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "0ETA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$T$", "MATH_0002": "$T$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{T_i \\to T\\}_{i \\in I}$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\subset T$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{U_j \\to U\\}_{j = 1, \\ldots, m}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\{T_i \\times_T U \\to U\\}_{i \\in I}$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-V-covering}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:75b9ce9a306ea3a59e0ef759b9d61c6b417ccabe12901a9dda85acac199f957c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4bb3f99ed16363803d3f86be2da771c73f47d27fd2b3bdec28cf9b191e4c29d1", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a scheme. A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>V covering of <MATH_0002><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is a family\nof morphisms <MATH_0003> of schemes such that for every\naffine open <MATH_0004> there exists a standard V covering\n<MATH_0005> refining the family\n<MATH_0006>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8e33cfea847307c195532da9e6e8ff3caf641166a3947502aa46adec30a70744", "unit_id": "tag:0ETH:statement"}
{"chapter": "topologies", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "0ETA", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F : \\Sch^{opp} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0002": "$F$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:db63225c15787d5197faf908fdebd1a943b6976e82a3b3edd87a53e06e675aaf", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8d6eb7b9c72f3aeee60a86bee9244b13c20a340ff6237af7b6c766f5d3e3c090", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe V topology has the same set theoretical problems as\nthe fpqc topology. Thus we refrain from defining V sites\nand we will not consider cohomology with respect to the V topology.\nOn the other hand, given a \n<MATH_0001>\nit does make sense to ask whether <MATH_0002> satisfies the sheaf property\nfor the V topology, see below.\nMoreover, we can wonder about descent of object\nin the V topology, etc.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:cda74897d4c62d8d5dd4ccded5a829264f4108e55512cbf762ff42c6a8788be5", "unit_id": "tag:0ETA:prose-0003"}
